---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = 'July 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — AI Betting Tips"
  description="What data we collect, how we use cookies and analytics, the third parties involved, and your rights over your personal data."
  active="">

  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-head">
      <div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span>Privacy Policy</div>
      <h1>Privacy <em>policy</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">This policy explains what information AI Betting Tips collects, why, and the choices you have. We keep data collection to a minimum.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      <div class="note"><strong>Template notice:</strong> this policy is a solid starting point for an affiliate content site, but it must be reviewed against your final analytics/cookie setup and the laws of the jurisdiction where you operate. Have a professional review it before launch.</div>

      <div class="toc">
        <a href="#who">Who we are</a>
        <a href="#collect">What we collect</a>
        <a href="#use">How we use it</a>
        <a href="#cookies">Cookies</a>
        <a href="#third">Third parties</a>
        <a href="#rights">Your rights</a>
        <a href="#retention">Retention &amp; security</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
      <p>AI Betting Tips (“we”, “us”) operates the website ai-betting-tips.com. The site is run by an independent publisher, and for data-protection purposes that publisher is the data controller. Registered company details will be published in this section as soon as a legal entity is incorporated; until then the controller is reachable directly at <a href="mailto:contact@ai-betting-tips.com">contact@ai-betting-tips.com</a>, which is a monitored address, not a form that goes nowhere.</p>
      <p>Write to that address for any data request — access, correction, deletion or objection — and say which you want. We answer these ourselves rather than routing them through a third party.</p>

      <h2 id="collect">What data we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Usage data</strong> — pages visited, approximate location (country), device and browser type, and referring site, collected in aggregate via analytics.</li>
        <li><strong>Cookies and similar technologies</strong> — see the cookies section below.</li>
        <li><strong>Information you send us</strong> — if you email us, we receive your email address and message so we can reply.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do <strong>not</strong> ask for or store betting-account credentials, payment details, or sensitive personal information. Registrations and deposits happen entirely on the operators' own sites, under their privacy policies.</p>

      <h2 id="use">How we use your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To operate, secure and improve the website and its content.</li>
        <li>To understand which pages and predictions are useful, in aggregate.</li>
        <li>To measure referrals to operators (so partners can attribute sign-ups) — see third parties.</li>
        <li>To respond to messages you send us.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Our legal bases are your consent (for non-essential cookies) and our legitimate interest in running and improving the site.</p>

      <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
      <p>Cookies are small files stored on your device. We use:</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Essential</td><td>Remember your theme choice and basic preferences so the site works. These cannot be switched off.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Analytics</td><td>Help us count visits and see how the site is used, in aggregate. Provider: <strong>[your analytics provider, e.g. Plausible / Google Analytics]</strong>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Affiliate</td><td>When you click through to an operator, a cookie or link parameter lets that operator credit the referral to us.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>You can control or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking some cookies may affect how the site works.</p>

      <h2 id="third">Third parties</h2>
      <p>We share limited data with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Analytics provider</strong> — to produce aggregate usage statistics.</li>
        <li><strong>Affiliate networks and operators</strong> — to attribute referrals when you choose to visit them.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting / infrastructure</strong> — our site is served through a hosting provider that may process technical logs (e.g. IP address) to deliver and protect the site.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We never sell your personal data.</p>

      <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live (for example under the UK/EU GDPR), you may have the right to access, correct, delete or restrict the processing of your personal data, to object to processing, and to data portability. To exercise any of these, email <a href="mailto:contact@ai-betting-tips.com">contact@ai-betting-tips.com</a>. You also have the right to complain to your local data-protection authority.</p>

      <h2 id="retention">Retention &amp; security</h2>
      <p>We keep analytics data only as long as needed to understand trends, and emails only as long as needed to handle your enquiry. We use reasonable technical measures to protect data, though no method of transmission over the internet is completely secure.</p>

      <h2 id="contact">Changes &amp; contact</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time; the “last updated” date above reflects the latest version. Questions? Email <a href="mailto:contact@ai-betting-tips.com">contact@ai-betting-tips.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
